The [[Mazar Clique]] or '''House of Masar''' refers to the merchant family that originated in [[Mazar]] that married into the [[Kingdom of Burawa]] that became the dominant ruling house after ascension of [[Iacob I]]. 

== History ==
The Mazar Clique started off as a wealthy Burawi-merchant family heralding from the city of [[Mazar]], their influence and power eventually lead them to the marriage between [[Appa of Mazar]] to [[Bugad the Great]], the prince of the [[Kingdom of Iskhal]]. The marriage lead to the formation of the [[Kingdom of Burawa]] under the [[Urtog Dynasty]], the [[Mazar Clique]] had continued to operate in parallel as an influential eye into the merchant class in the kingdom until the death of [[Dalgayan II]] in 573, where the family had influenced to place his great nephew [[Iacob I]] as the next King. The Mazar Clique's dynasty had continued then until the ascension of [[Marcel I]] of [[House Kadim]]